WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.479
Abraham: 'Hacking' is the process of
compromising and gaining unauthorised

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:10.420
access to a computer system or systems,
whole networks or digital devices and

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.350
taking control and inserting malware.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:16.929
This can be motivated by financial
gain, protest, information

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.050
gathering or just for the challenge!

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.121
Hackers can be from a range of backgrounds
and have different motives and may

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:23.669
include self-taught 'kids' or rogue IT
programmers and professionals skilled at

00:00:23.669 --> 00:00:24.219
modifying computer hardware and software.

00:00:24.219 --> 00:00:26.728
Hacking can involve technical skills
which can create “malvertising” or

00:00:26.728 --> 00:00:38.830
malicious advertising which uses online
advertising to spread and install malware.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:43.150
Hackers inject infected ads into
legitimate advertising networks that

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:44.970
display ads on trusted websites.

00:00:45.969 --> 00:00:49.690
But hackers also use psychology to
trick users into clicking on malicious

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:54.039
attachments or providing personal
data also known as social engineering.

00:00:54.769 --> 00:00:57.940
Hacking is an umbrella term which
covers a range of different cyber

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:01.870
attacks and has evolved from a lone
individual working from their bedroom

00:01:02.139 --> 00:01:05.600
to a widely established criminal
enterprise with turnkey hacking tools

00:01:05.889 --> 00:01:07.920
available to those with lesser skills.

00:01:08.179 --> 00:01:10.569
So, what motivates hackers
to commit their crimes.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:14.440
It may be financial gain such as
the theft of credit card details or

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.080
defrauding individuals and banks.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:18.450
Also holding companies to ransom.

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:23.009
It may be for gaining a reputation in
the hacker subculture by pulling off

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:24.999
hacks on sites and leaving their 'marks'

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:29.270
It may be for corporate espionage
where one company may hack another

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:33.500
to steal their information and gain a
marketplace advantage or individuals

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.060
will offer their services for sale.

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:39.040
It may be state sponsored with
nations stealing business, military

00:01:39.289 --> 00:01:43.190
or national intelligence secrets and
trying to destabilise other nations.

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:47.399
It may also involve Hacker Activists
or Hacktivists who are politically

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:51.750
or socially motivated and may wish to
raise public awareness and focus public

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:53.850
attention on something or someone.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:57.670
It’s important to remember that
an individual or a business may

00:01:57.670 --> 00:01:59.389
not always be the end target.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.550
You may even think why would
anyone want to hack me?

00:02:02.839 --> 00:02:04.599
But they may be a step along the way.

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:08.280
An individual or business may be hacked
because of the established connections

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.000
they have to a higher value target.

